  "body": "I think it'd be useful to add some guidance about how to do cross-browser testing to contributing.md, or maybe somewhere else like the wiki or WHATWG FAQ or something.\n\nMy main use case is that I want to be able to have somewhere easy to copy-and-paste this Markdown code from :)\n\n``` markdown\n| Test case                               | Edge | Chrome | Firefox | Safari\n|-----------------------------------------|------|--------|---------|-------|\n| Test case description 1                 | X    | X      |         |       |\n| Test case description 2                 | X    | X      |         |       |\n| Test case description 3                 | X    | X      |         |       |\n```\n\nI love issues with tables like that in them, but it's a pain to put together such tables unless you have a template.\n\nBut I think explaining some best practices like using live-dom-viewer or jsbin or web platform tests might also be good.\n",
